 "withdrawn": "k3v6 built with -DLNFOLD=0 (LayerNorm affine applied in registers instead of folded into the projection weights; both FASTSIG builds) returned NONDETERMINISTIC, WRONG outputs on an H100: over repeated launches on identical inputs, roughly 1 launch in 30-100 differs from the others with max|d| 2.3-4.8 vs the fp32 reference (correct launches 0.023-0.031). Observed at N = 200 (Np 208, the first sighting: the sealed-vector replay in a fresh process), 384, 768 and 1024, both directions, with and without mask, in five processes; it ALSO occurs with a host synchronisation after every launch and under CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1 (an intra-kernel fault, not a cross-launch hazard). In every located failure the wrong elements sit in ONE (tile, consumer warpgroup), in the last channel blocks (b = 6 or 7 of 8) and only in columns 16-31 of the 32-column block (accumulator-fragment registers e = 8..15) of a few rows. The same source built with NACC=1 (no wgmma group in flight during the epilogue), or with a different register split (CONS_REGS 240 / PROD_REGS 24), showed 0 differing launches in 468; the LNFOLD=1 builds (fastsig 0 and 1 \u2014 the k-trimul configuration of record folds the affine; 0-8 B local memory vs 336 B for LNFOLD=0) and the whole v6 route showed 0 differing launches in ~8000 (back-to-back, interleaved and host-synchronised protocols, N 200-2048). The evidence points at ptxas register allocation in the NACC=2 software pipeline under LNFOLD=0's register pressure (ptxas reports 508 B spill traffic and 'C7517 warpgroup.wait injected to allow use of registers defined by GMMA' for this build), not at the shared-memory / TMA protocol. The LNFOLD=0 cubins are therefore not shipped; python/face.py refuses lnfold=False by name. Evidence: the producer's determinism report (stress_k3.py / diag_k3.py tables)."
